Start by reading the task and its Related links to build context (use the glab CLI for GitLab URLs — run it from this repo so it authenticates). Give me a short summary of where the task stands and propose a first step, then help me work on it.

As we make progress, record it: tasq log 3 "<note>". If the status changes: tasq set 3 <in-progress|ready|waiting|blocked|later> [note]; priority: tasq set 3 <A|B|C>. Track the task's project directory with: tasq project 3 <path> (sessions start in the first tracked worktree that exists, otherwise there). Track development worktrees with: tasq worktree 3 <path>; to add a new worktree, declare its branch with: tasq worktree 3 <branch>, then create it with: tasq worktree up 3, which runs git worktree add. Track Claude sessions with: tasq session 3 <session-id> [desc], and merge requests with: tasq mr 3 <mr-url> [title]. When the task is finished, mark it done: tasq done 3 [note]. At the end of the session, run the /tasq:wrapup skill to record progress and final status.
